                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[quote][i]I was supplied with this key by the developer, this however did not affect the review.[/i][/quote]\n\nCalling all platformer fans- [b]Ubie has crash landed and he needs your help![/b] You must help your alien friend by going through levels and defeating enemies to find missing parts to his space ship. Along the way expect cuteness, humor and a lot of fun. This is a game great for children and those wanting a nostalgia fix.\n\nThe game play is simple. You can jump, double jump and float down with a balloon. Enemies are taken care of by jumping onto their heads, though they will respawn, so be careful. You bounce around collecting coins used to buy nifty add-ons like more music or changing Ubie’s color. The levels also offer goals of collecting bees to for the Queen Bee and there are hidden diamonds scattered about. The game is very straightforward and [b]easy to grasp[/b] but it still offers a challenge while the controls are intuitive and responsive.\n\nGraphics remind me of a flash game, they are rather simplistic and don’t offer much variety. Everything looks cute and colorful but that’s about it. This does not mean the graphics are bad.  For a simple platformer they work very well, but don’t expect bells and whistles. The game shines a bit more in the [b]up-beat and catchy music[/b] -I found myself playing levels to get more coins for songs.\n\nI would certainly recommend this game to anyone with children, especially if you want to get them into gaming. It’s a good casual experience for adults and easy to pick up and put down when you need a break. It has four worlds with plenty of levels, though they can be a bit short. My only issue is the price, I would advise you to [b]grab this title on sale[/b] since due to cost in relation to game length.\n\n\n[code]For more recommendations and reviews on our favourite up and coming quality games follow [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/LotsOGiveaways]Lot's O Giveaway's[/url] group curations [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/LotsOGiveaways#curation]here[/url]![/code]",
